# The same-frame bar for actions (PRD: "Actions: local result in the same frame"), with phase
# A's backend on a fixture store: each key is pressed through Broadway and timed from the
# command's handler to the list's change (rows removed, or the row's flags) and to the first
# frame painted after it. Each step fails when the change's p95 is over a 60 Hz frame
# (16.7 ms). Broadway paints without vsync, so its frame counts are printed, not judged.
# Run: tools/headless.sh 23 target/debug/sealwax --self-test tests/selftest/triage-frames.sealwax-test

desktop tiling
fixtures --count 400 --seed 13 --folders spread
resize 1440 900
triage-mark-read-on-open false
list-wait
focus list
list-select 0
measure-triage s 20
measure-triage e 20
measure-triage numbersign 10
measure-triage exclam 10
key <Shift>j 2
measure-triage s 10
measure-triage <Shift>u 1
measure-triage <Shift>i 1
measure-triage e 5
